{{/*
Generates ~/.config/chezmoi/chezmoi.toml on `chezmoi init`.

The machine profile is the only thing a human is ever asked. promptChoiceOnce
stores the answer in the generated config, so later runs of `chezmoi init` and
every `chezmoi apply` reuse it without asking again.

The profile is deliberately not derived from the hostname: the hostname is
chosen by the user during the Part 1 installer, so it says nothing reliable
about what kind of machine this is.

sourceDir is recorded because this project does not live where chezmoi would
put it by default: the source is the dotfiles/ directory of a clone of the whole
repository. Without it here, `chezmoi init --source` would work once and every
later `apply`, `edit` or `update` would look in ~/.local/share/chezmoi and find
nothing.
*/ -}}
{{- $machine := promptChoiceOnce . "machine" "Machine profile" (list "desktop" "laptop") -}}

sourceDir = {{ .chezmoi.sourceDir | quote }}

[data]
    machine = {{ $machine | quote }}
    laptop = {{ eq $machine "laptop" }}
